    {
      "id": "claim_ac1f7940bbb347f585378e85742f1277",
      "statement": "_update_lights() skips (warning logged once per 300 frames) when the EntertainmentStream is absent or disconnected, otherwise merges the zone colors onto channels via the zone-to-channel map — averaging xy per-component and integer-averaging brightness for every additional zone landing on the same channel — and dispatches the merged dict with one entertainment_stream.send_colors_xy() call. The REST client's per-light setters (HueBridge.set_light_color / set_light_gradient / set_zone_color) are used by Reading Mode for one-shot scene settings, not by the sync loop, so a dropped DTLS connection halts live updates rather than falling back to REST.",
